\title{Duality of conjunction and disjunction}
\date{2026-01-21T14:51:22Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{There's a good reason the symbols for [conjunction](002Z) and [disjunction](003F) are upside down versions of each
other: they are "opposite" (the mathy word is "dual") in the
sense that if we consider an opposite world where everything false
becomes true and vice versa, then #{\land} becomes #{\lor} and vice
versa.  Consider the following alternative definition of disjunction:

\transclude{003L}

Comparing to [the definition of conjunction](002Z), we can see that
they are identical but with all the \True's and \False's switched.}

